# Global Estates — Deployment

## Local
    npm install
    cp .env.example .env        # set DATABASE_URL (+ Stripe keys if available)
    npm start                   # schema auto-creates; seeds demo data when DB is empty
    open http://localhost:3000

## Deploy (Render example — works the same on Railway/Fly)
1. Push repo to GitHub → New → Web Service → connect repo.
2. Create a PostgreSQL instance → DATABASE_URL is injected automatically.
3. Env vars: JWT_SECRET, APP_URL=https://your-domain.onrender.com,
   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET, PLATFORM_FEE_PERCENT=5, CURRENCY=kes.
4. Build: `npm install` · Start: `npm start`. Tables + seed data are created on first boot.

## Stripe
- Use test-mode keys (sk_test_…). Test card: 4242 4242 4242 4242.
- Add webhook endpoint https://YOUR-DOMAIN/api/stripe/webhook with events:
  checkout.session.completed · checkout.session.expired · checkout.session.async_payment_failed
- Copy the signing secret into STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET and redeploy.
- Without STRIPE_SECRET_KEY the site still runs; checkout returns an explicit
  "Payment could not be started" error (no fake successes anywhere).

